    pr_ref:  # ae22
    description: "Hypergumbo currently ships four umbrella subcommands that overlap in purpose: `add-extras` / `remove-extras` (hand-coded sequential prints, covers grammars+gitleaks+embeddings+rust-analyzer, has the BUG-06 gate after PR #3603) and `install-extras` / `uninstall-extras` (declarative `_extras_components()` table, covers gitleaks+embeddings+rust-analyzer, has `--check` and `--skip` flags, but no BUG-06 gate). The overlap is tech debt — every new component has to be registered in both places, and drift caused rust-analyzer to silently fall off `add-extras` for some unknown stretch (surfaced today). The `install-extras` BUG-06 gap also produces a contradictory 'rust-analyzer ✓ installed' + BUG-06-runtime-error sequence, exactly the fragmented-investigation shape BUG-06 was filed to prevent.\n\nConsolidation:\n1. Extend `_extras_components()` to four rows (add grammars row at front; gate the rust-analyzer row's install with `is_rust_analyzer_integration_installed` so the table-driven path matches `cmd_install_rust_analyzer`).\n2. Rewrite `cmd_add_extras` table-driven; gain `--check` and `--skip` flags from install-extras.\n3. Rewrite `cmd_remove_extras` table-driven; gain `--skip`.\n4. Hard-remove `cmd_install_extras` / `cmd_uninstall_extras` and their argparse registrations. `hypergumbo install-extras` becomes 'invalid choice' (alpha-stage CLI breakage approved by user).\n5. Migrate test_install_extras.py cases into test_gitleaks.py; delete the file. Update test_help_output_order.\n6. CHANGELOG entry under Changed.\n\nSurface area inventory in plan file at /home/jgstern_agent/.claude/plans/spicy-snuggling-panda.md. Approved by user 2026-05-09."  # ae22
    fields: {}  # ae22
